            },
            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "Hi @klen, you can use `config` instead of `init` because `config` runs after the plugin is loaded. That way, you can safely call `require(\"mini.icons\").setup()` there and then apply the highlights. Everything will load in the correct order.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/klen/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/klen\">@klen</a>, you can use <code class=\"notranslate\">config</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">init</code> because <code class=\"notranslate\">config</code> runs after the plugin is loaded. That way, you can safely call <code class=\"notranslate\">require(\"mini.icons\").setup()</code> there and then apply the highlights. Everything will load in the correct order.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Hi @klen, you can use config instead of init because config runs after the plugin is loaded. That way, you can safely call require(\"mini.icons\").setup() there and then apply the highlights. Everything will load in the correct order.",
